{
  "about": "The owner-draft model's key table (spec 2026-11-24-workchat-polish §6.1): each case feeds its keys, one owner input chunk each, into an empty draft under its profile, and expects the model after the last one. Read by Go TestDraftFixture (internal/sessionhost/prompt_state_test.go) and Swift DraftModelFixtureTests (WatchtowerDesktop/Tests/Core): one rule on both sides, and FakeHostDelivery uses the Swift model. A case with \"app\" has the app's own delivery paste its line after that many keys: left typed (\"pause\": false) or in its pause before its Return through the case's last key (true); expect is the draft model then.",
  "claude_code_checked": "Claude Code 2.1.331, by hand in a pty on 2026-11-24: idle, one Ctrl+C over typed text cleared the input but showed 'Press Ctrl-C again to exit' (exit armed); working, one Ctrl+C interrupted the turn ('Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?') and the typed text stayed in the prompt. Neither just clears the input, so spec C11 applies: the owner's Ctrl+C makes the draft inexact for every profile. Ctrl+U, cursor at the end, then a marker line submitted to see what was left: a short single-line draft was erased whole; a 147-character draft wrapped over three rows of a 60-column pty lost only its last screen row (the submitted text began with the first two rows), so Ctrl+U makes the draft inexact too. One write of 'text\\r' to an idle prompt submitted it; Option+Return (ESC CR) inserted a line break (the submitted prompt had two lines).",
